<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The margin bar beside a paragraph that explains rather than sets: the rotate-button hint,
    the on-device-OCR caveat, the hold-to-back-up note.

    Those three used to look exactly like the switch labels above them, so a caveat read as one
    more thing you could turn on. The usual fixes are unavailable here — grey text dissolves on
    e-ink and italic costs real legibility in a four-line paragraph — so the demotion is
    positional instead: a rule down the left margin and an indent, the way a printed page marks
    an aside. Full ink, no reading cost, unmistakably not a control.

    A layer-list item with an explicit width pins the bar to the leading edge instead of letting
    the shape stretch across the whole background (API 23+; minSdk here is 26).
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:width="2dp" android:gravity="start|fill_vertical">
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@color/fgColor"/>
        </shape>
    </item>
</layer-list>
